<section class="section section--band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cards">

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">PhD students</p>
        <h3>Graduate students</h3>
        <p>
          Students join through the School of Biological Sciences at Georgia Tech,
          through <a href="https://biosciences.gatech.edu/phd-biology">Biology</a>, 
          <a href="https://qbios.gatech.edu/apply">Quantitative Biosciences (QBioS)</a>
          , or <a href="https://catalog.gatech.edu/programs/bioinformatics-phd/">Bioinformatics</a>.
          Applications are handled by the graduate programme, but write to me
          before you apply - I only admit people to the lab directly, not via rotations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tell me what you find interesting and why, what you want to work on, and how that fits into the Lab.
          A short, specific email beats a long, generic one. And make sure you attach a CV!
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Postdocs</p>
        <h3>Postdoctoral researchers</h3>
        <p>
          I am always glad to hear from prospective postdocs, particularly people
          interested in developing their own line of work within the lab's themes.
          Get in touch early if you are thinking about a fellowship, since the good
          ones close a long way in advance and the proposal is better when we write
          it together.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are two paths to postdoc opportunities in my lab. First, I may have 
          some funding to directly support a postdoc in my lab--please enquire to find
          out if that's the case at the moment. Second, I can help you develop 
          proposals for external fellowship support, such as the <em><a href="https://www.nsf.gov/funding/opportunities/prfb-postdoctoral-research-fellowships-biology">NSF postdoctoral research fellowships in biology (PRFB)</a></em> 
          which offers an <a href="https://www.nsf.gov/funding/opportunities/prfb-postdoctoral-research-fellowships-biology/nsf26-504/solicitation#awd_info">$85,000/year stipend and $25,000/year research and training funds</a>.
          I would be very excited to discuss research ideas with you for these opportunities!
        </p>


      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Undergraduates</p>
        <h3>Georgia Tech undergraduates</h3>
        <p>
          We take undergraduate researchers every semester, and several have gone
          on to publish peer-reviewed scientific papers and to present their research at international meetings. If you are a
          Georgia Tech student and this interests you, email me!
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
